cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you refer to this work, please cite the internship report as below."
title: "Differential Gene Expression Analysis of Head and Neck Squamous Cell Carcinoma (HNSC) Using RNA Sequencing Data"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Tanish N"
    affiliation: "Department of Biotechnology, Indira Gandhi College of Arts and Science, Puducherry"
date-released: "2026-11-20"
repository-code: "https://github.com/TanishDevs11/HNSC-RNAseq-Internship"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Cross-cohort transcriptomic pipeline integrating TCGA-HNSC tumour RNA-seq
  (482 primary tumour, 37 adjacent normal) with GTEx Esophagus Mucosa as
  surrogate normal tissue (273 samples). Covers identifier harmonisation
  (56,600 genes x 792 samples), exploratory PCA, ComBat-Seq batch correction,
  DESeq2 differential expression with apeglm shrinkage, and Reactome and
  ToppGene pathway enrichment, with explicit assessment of batch-condition
  confounding. Summer internship carried out at St. John's Research
  Institute, Bengaluru.
keywords:
  - head and neck squamous cell carcinoma
  - RNA-seq
  - TCGA
  - GTEx
  - batch effects
  - ComBat-Seq
  - DESeq2
  - pathway enrichment
preferred-citation:
